WEBVTT

00:27:27.646 --> 00:27:30.436
because I'm afraid
I won't be seen as a team player."

00:27:30.460 --> 00:27:33.316
And so they would say,
"Is there any research that you have

00:27:33.340 --> 00:27:37.351
that you could give me that maybe I could
show my boss in an empirical type of way?"

00:27:37.375 --> 00:27:39.464
And I thought,
"This is really interesting."

00:27:39.488 --> 00:27:40.967
So I started looking into it,

00:27:40.991 --> 00:27:43.270
and I found there was
this mountain of research.

00:27:43.294 --> 00:27:46.438
You know, and this is back in 2006, 2007.

00:27:46.462 --> 00:27:50.937
Lots of data showing that
when you have people in open offices,

00:27:50.961 --> 00:27:54.117
they're less productive,
they have trouble focusing.

00:27:54.141 --> 00:27:57.746
Ironically, they have more trouble
forming close connections,

00:27:57.770 --> 00:28:00.837
because if you think about it,